| Background / Queue  | Worker boundary             | Controlled retry / DLQ |


Determinism requires not only a failure boundary, but clear ownership of context.

HTTP-originated requests carry execution intent at the MVC action level.
When MediatR is absent, ExceptionFilters act as the enrichment boundary,
capturing action metadata and translating downstream exceptions into Result.Failure.

When MediatR is present, the Application pipeline owns failure normalization.
The request type itself represents execution intent, eliminating the need
for action-level enrichment.

Global middleware remains a safety net only, responsible for serialization,
never interpretation.

Each execution model defines a single owner of failure translation,
ensuring consistent, deterministic behavior regardless of request origin.
